  "criteria": "# DeepSeek DSpark at production settings: decision rule (fixed before measuring, 2026-10-20)\n\nUser request: retest DSpark for DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 Maya-S at the retained production\nsettings, since the earlier screening tested it only at 8 threads and 8K context.\n\nArms. Each uses a production-equivalent config (32K, `--tp 2` \u2192 layer groups on both XTX cards,\n`--reserve-mib 8192`, `--cpu-threads 24`) and its own copy of the production expert-routing\nprofile, so all arms start from the same seed and production state is never modified.\n- A1 production: `--dspark none`\n- B candidate: identical, plus `--dspark on`\n- A2 production again, to measure drift\n\nEach arm is served by `hardware/serve-maya-candidate.py` (guards, at least 6 GiB whole-card startup\nheadroom, no-swap), then runs `validate-maya.py` (functional, tools and ~7K retrieval) and\n`benchmark-maya-selection.py` (3 excluded warmups + 3 timed 128-output requests per task).\n\nKeep DSpark (switch production to `--dspark on`) ONLY IF B passes every check and guard, AND,\nagainst the mean of A1 and A2:\n- the geometric mean of {code decode, prose decode, native ~7K prefill} improves by at least 5%, and\n- no single metric is more than 5% worse.\n\nOtherwise production stays `--dspark none`. The DSpark draft weights stay on disk either way.\n",
